{"reference":"Psalms 90","book":"Psalms","chapter":90,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Note on Psalm Headings","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The received superscriptions in Psalms associate various psalms with figures such as David, Asaph, Solomon, Moses, Heman, and Ethan. They also preserve labels for genres, performance, tunes, instruments, and narrative settings. Because the status and interpretation of these headings are disputed, they should be considered carefully rather than treated as straightforward narrative statements.","verse_refs":["Psalms 90:1"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_090_f3a6488c75ec28e637b9f636"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}